{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6SMVw6", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": true, "path": "tests/facility/patient/encounter/encounterPlannedStatusTransition.spec.ts", "line": 98, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 87, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 90, "originalStartLine": 87, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7XXEX-", "body": "These tests create/update encounters for a shared patient and can hit backend limits (you already note the 5-live-encounter limit). Since Playwright is configured with `fullyParallel: true`, the tests in this file may run concurrently and become flaky; run this describe in serial mode.", "createdAt": "2026-07-20T09:11:43Z", "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T09:11:44Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6SOtPB", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": true, "path": "tests/facility/patient/encounter/encounterPlannedStatusTransition.spec.ts", "line": 99, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 96, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 95, "originalStartLine": 92, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7XaT5J", "body": "This suite relies on per-test inline cleanup, but if a test fails before reaching its cleanup step the encounter can remain live and later runs can start failing due to the 5-live-encounter-per-patient limit (which the file comments already call out). A best-effort afterEach cleanup makes the suite more resilient.", "createdAt": "2026-07-20T11:42:54Z", "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T11:42:54Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6SOtPW", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": true, "path": "src/components/Questionnaire/QuestionTypes/EncounterQuestion.tsx", "line": null, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": null, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 179, "originalStartLine": 175, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7XaT5o", "body": "The end-date normalization logic depends on `encounter.period.start/end` (future-start special-casing), but the effect only re-runs on `encounter.status` changes. If the user edits the start date after choosing a status (e.g., sets Cancelled then changes start to a future date), this effect won\u2019t rerun and can leave an invalid period (start > end).", "createdAt": "2026-07-20T11:42:54Z", "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T11:42:54Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6SOv9G", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": true, "path": "tests/facility/patient/encounter/encounterPlannedStatusTransition.spec.ts", "line": null, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": null, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 39, "originalStartLine": 33, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7XaXnG", "body": "`page.waitForURL()` is awaited after clicking \u201cCreate Encounter\u201d, which can race with fast navigations and lead to flaky failures. Wrap the click + wait in `Promise.all` so the listener is registered before the navigation starts.", "createdAt": "2026-07-20T11:45:34Z", "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T11:45:35Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6SPkjy", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "tests/facility/patient/encounter/encounterFormHelpers.ts", "line": 12, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 12, "startDiffSide": null, "originalLine": 12, "originalStartLine": null, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7XbgNb", "body": "`page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Patient Home\" }).click()` can fail in Playwright strict mode if multiple \"Patient Home\" links are present (other specs already use `.first()` for this selector). To keep this helper robust across the app shell/nav, pick the first match explicitly.", "createdAt": "2026-07-20T12:37:57Z", "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T12:37:57Z", "author": {"login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6YjLiY", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "src/components/Questionnaire/QuestionTypes/EncounterQuestion.tsx", "line": 194, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 192, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 194, "originalStartLine": 192, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7geEgP", "body": "Adding `encounter.period.end` to the deps of an effect that *writes* `period.end` is how you get feedback loops and stomped user input. The guards make it converge, sure \u2014 but the real damage is UX: now the user can never clear the end date on a Discharged/Completed encounter, because this effect will slam it right back in on the next render. Watch `period.start` if you must, but leave `period.end` out of it.", "createdAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "author": {"login": "github-actions"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6YjLia", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "src/components/Questionnaire/QuestionTypes/EncounterQuestion.tsx", "line": 145, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 144, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 145, "originalStartLine": 144, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7geEgR", "body": "`new Date(encounter.period.start)` with zero validation. If `start` is ever a partially-typed or malformed string you get `Invalid Date`, every comparison returns `false`, and the code silently decides \"not in the future\" and stamps an end date the backend will reject. Check `!isNaN(d.getTime())` \u2014 or use the date util this codebase already ships \u2014 before trusting it.", "createdAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "author": {"login": "github-actions"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6YjLie", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "src/components/Questionnaire/QuestionTypes/EncounterQuestion.tsx", "line": 190, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 163, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 190, "originalStartLine": 163, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7geEgV", "body": "Four near-identical `handleUpdateEncounter({ period: { ...encounter.period, end: X } })` blocks in one effect. *Sighs in DRY principle.* Compute the desired end value once (`undefined` / `now` / keep), compare it to `encounter.period.end`, and dispatch a single update. Same behaviour, a third of the lines, and the next person to touch the status rules won't have to fix the same bug in four places.", "createdAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T11:31:36Z", "author": {"login": "github-actions"}}]}}
{"id": "PRRT_kwDODtfaXs6kDfEl", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "src/components/Questionnaire/QuestionTypes/EncounterQuestion.tsx", "line": 192, "diffSide": "RIGHT", "startLine": 183, "startDiffSide": "RIGHT", "originalLine": 192, "originalStartLine": 183, "resolvedBy": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"id": "PRRC_kwDODtfaXs7xrliA", "body": "Per the HL7 FHIR spec, a cancelled encounter is structurally defined as having ended before it has begun. Because it never actually started, providing a period.end (which implies a chronological conclusion to an active clinical event) is incorrect. The cancellation state itself satisfies the end of the lifecycle.", "createdAt": "2026-09-19T21:10:14Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-19T21:10:17Z", "author": {"login": "bodhish"}}]}}

