L107: Comments  | Different use-cases are likely to have different permitted transitions between states, such as an Emergency department could use `arrived` when the patient first presents, then `triaged` once has been assessed by a nurse, then `receiving-care` once treatment begins, however other sectors may use a different set of these values, or their own custom set in place of this example valueset provided.
L108: Encounter.episodeOfCare
L109: Element Id  | Encounter.episodeOfCare
L110: Definition  | Where a specific encounter should be classified as a part of a specific episode(s) of care this field should be used. This association can facilitate grouping of related encounters together for a specific purpose, such as government reporting, issue tracking, association via a common problem.
L111: The association is recorded on the encounter as these are typically created after the episode of care and grouped on entry rather than editing the episode of care to append another encounter to it (the episode of care could span years).
L112: Short Display  | Episode(s) of care that this encounter should be recorded against
